    {
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-109518 requires APT to acquire and install packages over attacker-controlled HTTP while following redirects and retrying downloads. The shipped Extra CODEOWNERS entrypoint, healthcheck, migrations and application routes run Python; they do not invoke APT, load its Python bindings or expose its package-acquisition API. GitHub requests use HTTPX, not APT. The vulnerable APT acquisition/install code is therefore outside the reviewed service execution path. The apt packages remain present and unpatched. This assessment does not cover operator-run package installation, custom code or plugins, or arbitrary execution after compromise.",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
